{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"GATE FAIL\n\n1. **C4 still lets one scenario borrow another’s forecast.** I swapped G2’s low and high company forecasts in the Data Center calculations, recomputed both values, and the checker accepted the crossed pair. I also made R1b pass by putting the $108B guide in an alternate forecast and letting the base scenario use it. **Fix:** require each point calculation to use the shared forecast for its own scenario. Let the final range summarize the checked scenarios. Add the crossed G2 and alternate-scenario R1b cases as refusals. [C4 checker](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:380), [G2 fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:222)\n\n2. **An earlier figure can still become the current forecast.** I set v9’s current outcome to the authenticated `$414B` prior figure. Both the rendered schema and the checker accepted it. C10 checks whether a prior feeds another figure, so using it directly as the outcome bypasses the check. **Fix:** apply the comparison-only rule to answer outcomes as well as calculation inputs. Add a case that uses a valid prior as the current outcome and require C10 to refuse it. [Outcome and prior checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:321)"}}
